## Accepted direction

- 2026-10-04: ACCEPTED CORE LOOP - roll PART OFFERS (the roll never grants a part) -> buy with Snow or reserve -> build a SNOWPLOW (blade / engine / running gear) -> drive through the fields -> earn Snow and treasures -> improve the vehicle. Snowplows replace the orbiting shovels as the digging mechanic; the shovel game is kept and restorable with ReplicatedStorage.PlowConfig.Mode = "Legacy" (archive: ServerStorage.LegacyArchive_2026-10-04). Odds, prices, cooldowns and vehicle balance are all in PlowConfig. Pacing still needs a tuning pass (see STATUS.md).
- 2026-10-03: never lock upgrades behind stages; pace them with price (UpgradeConfig U.StageBudgetShare).
- 2026-10-03: the lobby huts are replaced by machines (Shovel Forge, Hot Cocoa Machine, Pet Fuser). Build their models in Blender (World2Blender pipeline), not from Studio parts.
A bright, cartoony snow-digging/RNG simulator for kids and teens: roll shovels, dig Snow, buy upgrades, collect pets and treasures, unlock biomes and rebirth. Keep progression varied, with readable silhouettes, colorful landmarks and playful feedback.

- **Latest pacing target (2026-10-02):** fast start, slower later; World 1, ending at the Absolute Zero Portal, should take **more than 3 hours without paid boosts**. Claude's latest model includes events, daily rewards, quests and achievements: about 4 hours for an efficient engaged solo player, about 5 hours casual, about 6 hours ignoring rewards. These are model estimates, not measured human playthroughs.
- Art: simple attractive, chunky rounded 3D models; snowy ground, icy blue shadows, warm hut lighting. User requested Blender scenery across all eight World 1 stages. The AllStages pack remains prepared; consult STATUS.md before importing or replacing scenery.
- **Frostfall Village is the approved active lobby.** Preserve the archived original in ServerStorage.OldLobbyBackup.
- **Snowy GUI approved (2026-10-03):** use the generated snowy panel/card/button treatment across existing menus, HUD, Rewards, tutorial, prompts and loading, while preserving gameplay callbacks, real pet/egg viewports and existing collection art. **User explicitly excluded the upgrade screen; leave UpgradeTreeGui/UpgradeTreeClient unchanged.** Only the floating egg/chances outer background stays fully transparent. Art, prompts, source/property backups and verification: outputs/SnowyUI20261003/README.md.
- The earlier egg redesign was rejected. Seven later Blender biome eggs form the current hatchable lobby display; do not reinstall rejected designs.
- User wants requested work implemented in the game, unless they explicitly request only a prompt.
- Preserve unrelated work, ownership IDs, player progress, and recoverable replacements. Do not publish or reset real player data without explicit instruction.

- **World 2 layout (user feedback 2026-10-03: not one straight line; bigger distant mountains):** winding chain of floating islands. Each stage = 260 x 100 island, then a 60-stud themed S-curve bridge (stride 320 along +X). Island west edges / centre Z / ground Y: Sakura 1565 / 0 / 0, Candy 1885 / +55 / +4, Atlantis 2205 / -15 / -10, planned Toybox 2525 / +45 / -2, Clockwork 2845 / -35 / +6, Cloud 3165 / +25 / +22, Neon 3485 / -40 / +10, Cosmic 3805 / +10 / +34. Each gate sits at the previous island's exit; the bridge lands in an opening of the next island's west wall. Background = big themed mountain ranges (~690 long, 150-320 tall, base ~120-170 below the islands) in two layers each side (Workspace.World2.Horizon), not single peaks.

- **Fog between maps (user request 2026-10-03):** each crossing has a CloudCurtain (opaque puffy cloud bank, ~32 x 311 x 431 studs, Workspace.World2.CloudCurtains) at the bridge middle so the next island is hidden, plus a 'Mist' lighting zone over the bridge (Atmosphere density 0.62, near-white). Mountains: natural massifs (rounded summits, ridges, conforming snow, foothills; Horizon v2 asset 119627339956378): themed near layer at z +/-440 centred on each stage, neutral hazy 'DistantRange' far layer at +/-680; never thin cone peaks.

- **Natural, asymmetric planting (user feedback 2026-10-03: stages looked too symmetrical, trees one size in perfect rows):** place trees/bushes/coral in groves of 1-3 with gaps, sizes ~0.7-1.6x, random rotation, different density per side, staggered (not mirrored) lamp rows, and at least one one-sided focal cluster per stage. Landmarks/gates may stay symmetric.

- **Every stage gets its own layout + dense detail (user feedback 2026-10-03: 'more detail, different layout, it's getting boring'):** do NOT reuse the template of two long fields on both sides of a straight central path. Vary field shapes/positions (any axis-aligned boxes, e.g. diagonal corners, different sizes), give each stage districts or levels (terraces + stairs, canals, plazas), a central or off-centre set piece, moving life (vehicles/creatures on Loop/Orbit, spinning parts, particles such as chimney steam) and street-level props (benches, barrels, signs, planters, bunting). Edges: themed walls ~3 players high. Clockwork City v2 is the reference.

- **No coplanar surfaces (z-fighting fix 2026-10-03):** island bodies/rims must top out >= 0.1 stud BELOW the stage floor; layered flat pieces (rugs, inlays, water vs basin, knobs) need >= 0.05 stud height steps; overlapping wall segments alternate a 0.18 stud depth + 0.04 stud height offset. Check with the coplanar-surface scan (see STATUS batch 15).

- **Stage size (user request 2026-10-03: a little shorter and wider):** islands are now 234 x 110 (were 260 x 100); island centres unchanged; bridges 86 studs. Built island x-ranges / centre z / floor y: Sakura 1565-1812 (247 long, west end kept for the arrival plaza) / 0 / 0, Candy 1898-2132 / 55 / 4, Atlantis 2218-2452 / -15 / -10, Toybox 2538-2772 / 45 / -2, Clockwork 2858-3092 / -35 / 6; planned Cloud 3178-3412 / 25 / 22, Neon 3498-3732 / -40 / 10, Cosmic 3818-4052 / 10 / 34. Standard fields 120 x 33 at centre z +/-25; invisible side walls at +/-55.5.


- **World 2 = 7 stages (user decision 2026-10-03: skip Neon):** Sakura, Candy, Atlantis, Toybox, Clockwork, Cloud, Cosmic Sanctuary (final). Neon Dream City is dropped; Cosmic was moved into its slot: x 3498-3732, centre z 10, floor y 34, gate (crescent MoonArch x0.55 + violet paywall) at the Cloud exit (3412, 22, 25), 86-stud starry bridge, fog bank at (3455.5, 28, 17.5). Cosmic uses the stage-15 pacing step: stage 13Qi, Star Egg 1.3Qi (pets 18.7-111.7), tiles 26/20.8/13/16.9Qi, fields TileHP 4.8M / SnowPerPhase 142.6M. The Coming Soon gateway at Cosmic's east end is the end of World 2.

## Current systems — verified from Studio on 2026-10-02

| Area | Current behavior and source |
|---|---|
| World 1 balance | Stage costs: Desert 2.5K, Cursed 250K, Crystal 54M, Retro 4B, Jungle 135B, Absolute Zero 2.5T, Portal 150T Snow. Stage eggs, rebirth milestones and stage-locked upgrades were scaled with the balance pass. StageConfig / PetConfig / RebirthConfig / UpgradeConfig. |
| Upgrades | **110 tiles**, across Snow, Rolls and Misc. Explicit costs/stage locks; IDs preserve purchases. Luck tiles add percentages; shovels contribute neutral x1 luck. Balance.PowerExponent=0.63. Golden Dice starts every 10 rolls, improves to 5 (x3 luck); Rainbow starts every 100, improves to 50 (x10). |
| Rebirth | +0.50 Snow and +0.25 luck per rebirth, additive, cap 50. Resets Snow/stages/upgrades while retaining pets, shovels and discoveries. First milestone: Cursed + 62K Snow. RebirthConfig / RebirthService / RebirthRules. |
| Pets and eggs | **7 hatchable eggs, 35 pets**, including Retro/Jungle/AbsoluteZero. PetConfig / PetModels / PetService / StarterGui.RNGGui.PetClient. FrostfallVillage.EggDisplay contains the world eggs; EggFloat animates them. PetClient shows nearest odds and clones the Shell for hatching. |
| Shovel mutations | Giant: 1 in 5, x2 size/reach. Shiny: 1 in 10, x3 power. Shiny Giant combines them. RNGConfig / RNGHandler / ShovelOrbit / SnowFieldService. Index has Normal/Giant/Shiny/Shiny Giant tabs. |
| Snow fields | Workspace.SnowFieldZones defines Edit-time boxes; SnowFieldData and tiles are built during Play. SnowFields / SnowFieldService / SnowFieldClient. Sakura has its own template and two zones. |
| Buried Treasures | Fully dug tiles roll 1/100; first treasure guaranteed on the third tile. 7 biome sets, 5 rarities, 35 collection items; average Snow bonus about 6% of digging income. Collection survives rebirth. **36 PNG slots are populated** (35 treasures + menu chest). TreasureConfig / TreasureIcon / TreasureModels chest fallback / TreasureService / TreasureBook / TreasureReveal. Luck does not change these odds. Art: outputs/TreasureIcons20261001/generated-20261002/. |
| Rewards / Activities | New REWARDS left-menu button and panel with Daily, Quests, Achievements and Codes. 7-day rewards, 3 quests with a 30-minute refresh after all claims, **19 permanent-bonus achievements**, server events Snowstorm/Lucky Wind/Aurora about every 10–15 minutes. ActivityConfig / ActivityService / BoostService / ActivityClient. Codes live server-side in ActivityService. Profile fields d.Activity and d.SnowEarned; UpgradeService applies Snow/luck boosts. |
| World 2 | **Approved lineup (2026-10-02): 8 stages = global 9-16:** Sakura Garden, Candy Kingdom, Sunken Atlantis, Giant Toybox, Clockwork City, Cloud Kingdom, Neon Dream City, Cosmic Sanctuary; ~260 x 100 studs each along +X from x=1565, connected by themed paid gates; each with 2 fields, egg + 5 Blender pets, 5 treasures, stage upgrades and one small activity. Sakura opens with Portal (Cost 0). StageService streams/teleports; World 2 respawn returns to the Sakura plaza. **Blender import route:** w2lib.py -> FBX -> Open Cloud upload (env ROBLOX_API_KEY) -> insert_asset -> ServerStorage.World2Templates (see STATUS.md). Blender pets live in ReplicatedStorage.PetModelOverrides. |
| Intro / starter shovel | About 7.9-second lobby storyboard: sky fall, landing, shovel discovery/grab, two-handed victory, close-up, gameplay handoff. Existing **Tin Shovel**, the least rare base shovel; StarterShovelRules grants it once per eligible profile and preserves better equipment. SnowIntroController / SnowIntroRig / SnowIntroArt / SnowIntroService / SnowIntro bootstrap. Skip and Studio I replay retained. ReplicatedFirst.LoadingScreen covers joining. |
| Tutorial / lobby | TutorialClient: roll, collect 10 Snow, open upgrades; prefers FrostfallSnowYard. Lobby origin (−105, 0.24, −282), spawn near (−167, 0.32, −282). FrostfallClient / FrostfallTravel / VillageOpenMenu. Cabins have repaired rear gables; paths join; snow globe uses existing Gold and Absolute Zero shovel models. |
| Upgrade UI | **UpgradeTreeClient v3**: Snow/Rolls share the main branch, Misc link/back switches pages. Owned + attached frontier + mystery ring; one-tap buying, green affordable/red unaffordable/blue owned. Larger PNG icons; preserves UpgradeTreeGui name for tutorial. Studio-only. |
| Sound | RollController has crisp prize-wheel ticks, speed-based pitch, landing click, quieter mini mode. RNGGui attributes RollTickVolume / RollTickOff control them. Studio-only; consult sound handoffs before changing asset IDs. |
| Lighting / scenery | ReplicatedFirst.BiomeLighting + Profiles grade areas, including Sakura; Lighting.BiomeGrade. FrostfallLobbyDecor / CursedStageDecor / StageDecor20260930 contain current scenery. StageDecorClient animates nearby bob/Water/Sway/Orbit/Roll props and culls distant particles. Earlier scene counts are historical; inspect current objects. |

## Source mirroring, Rojo and Graphify

The 2026-10-02 refresh captured current Edit sources: **45 scripts in game/src** for ReplicatedStorage, ServerScriptService and StarterPlayerScripts, plus **23 read-only scripts in game/studio-snapshots** for StarterGui, ReplicatedFirst, Workspace and active ServerStorage helpers. Two generic Workspace.Script copies are archive-only. The source manifest records actual classes, RunContext, paths and hashes.

- default.project.json maps only ReplicatedStorage, ServerScriptService and StarterPlayerScripts. StarterGui, Workspace, ServerStorage and ReplicatedFirst remain Studio-managed.
- A Workspace Script may use RunContext=Client; check the snapshot manifest rather than inferring execution from its filename.
- The SnowStages folder now preserves unknown Studio children so an unmapped Sakura template is retained. Existing stage economic attributes matched disk.
- Existing binary .rbxm models were not re-exported or verified. Sakura geometry/template, GUI hierarchy, lighting instances and map models remain in Studio. This folder cannot rebuild the full place.
- No active Rojo server/plugin connection was verified during this refresh. Before connecting, verify the server serves this canonical folder and review its proposed changes. Never connect the historical ca/game server or let old disk sources overwrite newer Studio work.
- **Laptop Claude chat:** its uploaded files are static copies. After a refresh, re-upload the latest PROJECT.md, STATUS.md, graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md and graph.json, or use the handoff ZIP. No automatic memory sharing.
- Graphify scans game/ only. For code questions, query the scoped graph first; then verify live sources. Refresh snapshots after Studio edits, then run Refresh-Graph.ps1. A disk-only rebuild cannot capture live changes.
- Latest graph (2026-10-04 after new shovel icon/source mirroring): **562 nodes, 1,083 edges, 49 communities**. Earlier extraction warned about partial parsing in UpgradeTreeClient and PortalAnimator around Luau compound assignments. Graphify is navigation aid, not a Roblox compiler or runtime test.

## Tests, recovery and current limits

Shovel icon artwork: 49 base shovels now include 14 new Blender shovels with generated transparent 512px PNG icons. RNGConfig ImageId is shared by ItemIcon across rolls/index/inventory and inherited by all Giant/Shiny variants. Artwork, prompts, comparison gallery and recovery: outputs/NewShovelIcons20261004/README.md.

Reusable VFX: ReplicatedStorage.UniversalVFX has 10 small tintable PNG textures and 9 presets; user requested simple low-poly-inspired effects with 256px particles / 512px rings. The forge uses the new flame/smoke/streak bindings; its existing timings/colors/lights stay in their original system. ServerStorage.UniversalVFX_Showcase previews the library; backup emitters are in UniversalVFXBackup20261004. Art, prompts, usage and verification: outputs/UniversalVFX20261003/README.md.

Prefer Studio tools for live changes and re-read affected sources before applying prepared patches because Claude and Codex can share the place. Workspace contains duplicate names; a dot path may be ambiguous.

For isolated progression tests, set ServerStorage.BalanceTestMode=true in **Edit before Play**, stop only your own Play session afterward, and remove the attribute in Edit. It isolates the main DataService, not every third-party system. Direct MCP module requires/test hooks can be blocked by Studio command capabilities; do not weaken those capabilities.

Latest recovery/export evidence: outputs/StudioRefresh20261002/ (live source archive, per-source hashes, before copies and sync report). Claude balance backups: ServerStorage.BalanceBackups.Before_20261002_FastStart / Before_20261002_Activities / Before_20261002_Balance_v2. Older art, lobby and intro backups remain recoverable; never blindly rerun historical builders.

Open issues and the next checks are at the top of STATUS.md. Implemented, tested, saved and published states must be stated separately.
